      "text": "Closest rival: two four-carrier trolley trips, 0-3 and 3-6, followed by hand-carrying B12 at 6-7. Completion-first boundary ordering allows both full unloads and the final hand unload without waiting. Prediction: the same complete release outcome, seven occupied transfer minutes, thirteen inspection minutes, peak rack occupancy five, two consumed allowances. Present separating probe: replay both schedules against boundary rules and, for whichever is executed, record identities, releases, counts, occupied intervals, rack states and charge use with R6. Nine versus seven transfer minutes separates their present burden claims."
